  "body": "This change extends the ES Script Modules system to include CSS module scripts. These will allow web developers to load CSS into a component definition in a manner that interacts seamlessly with other module script types.\r\n\r\n[Explainer document](https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/css-modules-v1-explainer.md)\r\n[Discussion thread](https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/issues/759)\r\n\r\nThis PR includes the integration for the [import assertions](https://github.com/tc39/proposal-import-assertions/) TC39 proposal. I plan to land that integration as a separate PR (https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/5883/), but those changes are included here as well since CSS module script depends on them.\r\n\r\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\r\n   * Chromium: [Implemented behind a flag](https://chromestatus.com/feature/5948572598009856)\r\n   * Firefox: https://github.com/mozilla/standards-positions/issues/541\r\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/tree/master/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/css-module\r\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/master/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\r\n   * Chromium: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=992499\r\n   * Firefox: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1720570\r\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=227967\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\r\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\r\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\r\n\r\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\r\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\r\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\r\n    and remove what's below.\r\n-->\r\n***\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/1bec6ad...a879a84/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/1bec6ad...a879a84/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">/references.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/1bec6ad...a879a84/references.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">/scripting.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/1bec6ad...a879a84/scripting.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/timers-and-user-prompts.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">/timers-and-user-prompts.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/1bec6ad...a879a84/timers-and-user-prompts.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">diff</a> )\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">/webappapis.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/4898/1bec6ad...a879a84/webappapis.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 14, 2021, 6:25 PM UTC (a879a84)\">diff</a> )",
